MODIFICATIONS
=============

Per Apache License 2.0 section 4(b), the following files were modified from
their upstream versions:

  bin/qbo-write
    Added a warning that the MCP server name this script is registered under
    is load-bearing for the confirmation gate's matcher.

  src/types/tool-definition.ts
    Replaced the handler type with a structural signature. The MCP SDK's
    ToolCallback generic exceeds TypeScript's instantiation depth when indexed
    (TS2589), which made three test suites fail to compile.

  src/helpers/register-tool.ts
    Calls server.tool() through a structural type for the same TS2589 reason,
    and wraps READ tool handlers with the response sanitizer described below.

  tests/unit/helpers/register-tool.test.ts
    Updated for the above; the previous handler-identity assertion no longer
    holds for READ tools, which are now wrapped.

The following files are new in this distribution:

  bin/qbo-confirm-hook                       Claude Code PreToolUse hook
  src/helpers/mutation-tiers.ts              risk tiers, name normalization
  src/helpers/describe-mutation.ts           plain-English mutation summaries
  src/helpers/sanitize-qbo-text.ts           untrusted-text delimiting + flags
  tests/unit/bin/qbo-confirm-hook.test.ts
  tests/unit/helpers/mutation-tiers.test.ts
  tests/unit/helpers/describe-mutation.test.ts
  tests/unit/helpers/sanitize-qbo-text.test.ts

No upstream tool, handler, or QuickBooks API behaviour was changed. The tool
catalogue is unchanged: 141 tools with writes enabled, 70 in read-only mode.
